WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.667
♪♪

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.601
-Whoa!
-Wow!

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.300
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.067
That's --

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.534
You know what?
-I'm so confused.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.834
-That's a lot of love.
-Yeah, that's so sweet.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.267
I'm, like, genuinely
taken aback.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:17.067
-Yeah, good.
-I don't know what to do now.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:20.267
-I feel that way, too, though.
You've been on our show once,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.000
but I feel like
I want to be friends with you.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.033
I love you.
-Should we?

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.367
-Yeah.
-Done.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.367
-You want to?
-Yeah.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.033
Cool.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:31.834
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.667
You totally did it.
I know, I know.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.534
How is "Saturday Night Live"
going?

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:37.734
-It's going really well,
actually.

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.834
Everyone is really cool.
It's very comfortable.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.234
I feel like I'm still --

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.534
I forget that they've been
doing it for so long.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.334
So, like,
things happen so quickly.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:48.534
-Oh, yeah. -We were deciding
the sketches the other day,

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.167
and I remember
I was sitting in the chair

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.400
across from Lorne Michaels,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.400
and everyone started
getting up and leaving.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.367
And I looked at Lorne, and I was
like, "Oh, are we done?"

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.734
And he was like, "Yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.567
-"Yeah, we moved on."
-I was sitting there

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:00.968
for maybe 30 seconds.
Like, it did not feel --

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.534
-There's no more scripts
to read. That's it.

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:03.734
-We go through things
so quickly.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.100
-Is it because
you're savoring every moment?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.434
-Maybe, I guess you could say.

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.567
But also, at the same time,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.434
I'm so in awe
of everybody around me.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.400
I'm also,
I guess, being really quiet.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.434
I was looking at,
as we were taking the sketches,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:15.868
he was like,
"Is there a sketch you prefer?

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.000
This one or this one?"

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.234
I said, "Oh, I think
that one's funnier,"

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.968
and he said, "Okay.
Well, then say something."

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.300
And I was like, "Oh!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.734
-That's right. Exactly right.
-"Yeah, you're right."

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.434
-Obviously, you learned
some lessons

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:25.901
out of "Saturday Night Live."
-I think I'm learning.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.200
I'm picking up on it now.
-Yeah, it's the best crew

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.434
up there, the best writers,
the best hair and makeup.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.501
It's so much fun.
-Yeah, they're so seasoned.

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.701
-Yeah, it's great.
You're gonna be fantastic.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.000
Break a leg this Saturday.
Come on.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
We'll be watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.934
We'll be watching
and supporting.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.434
Last time we were here, we were
talking about "Wednesday."

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.868
And, man, oh, man, it turned out
one of the biggest shows

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.167
in the world on Netflix.
So, congratulations.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:51.100
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.067
-And since you've been here,
it got picked up for season two,

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.100
so there you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.667
More work.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.934
Work breeds work.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.434
Now you're gonna work more.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:03.334
No, I'm very excited.
-Do you have any idea

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.100
where you're gonna go
this season at all?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.000
-I don't know.
I think we just started

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.200
getting a writers room together
and kind of talking about it.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.567
And everyone's
being really cool.

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.434
I think we want to up kind of
the horror aspect of it

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.467
a little bit
and then get Wednesday

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.601
out of the romantic situation
and just let her be her own

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.868
individual
and fight her own crime.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:24.367
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:27.167
You've been nominated
for every single award.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.734
Congratulations.
Well-deserved.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.634
-Thank you.
-Really. Can't get enough.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:35.067
Do you like going to these award
shows and doing the whole thing?

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.133
-I don't think --
going to award shows,

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.501
the 30 minutes before,
it's the most sick

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.000
you'll ever feel
in your entire life.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.767
You're so anxious, so nervous,
so whatever, and especially --

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.033
You're with people
that you admire.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.367
Like, the SAG Awards, it was,
you know, all of your peers,

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:50.634
everyone who's a part of SAG,

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:51.801
so you're seeing
these people like --

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.167
-You had a hot table.
I loved your table.

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:54.467
-Yeah, I had
a really cool table.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:57.434
-Yeah, Zendaya was there.
-Yeah, well, Zendaya,

00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:00.167
I feel like we've kind of --
we've met and not met

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.567
so many times, I feel like,
this time, we were actually

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.133
able to have
a nice conversation.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.534
But I was kind of freaking out
because she was sitting

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:08.901
next to Paul Mescal, who I think
is so talented and so good.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.100
And I was so nervous
to meet him,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.634
and I knew he was gonna
be at my table.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.868
And I remember him --
he introduced himself to me

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.601
when I wasn't expecting it.
-Ooh.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.067
-So he was like,
"Oh, hi! Nice to meet you.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.567
I'm Paul."
And I was so nervous,

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:19.801
I kind of couldn't
look him in the eye,

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:21.267
so I fear that
it was a bit like --

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.501
-You were like, "Yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah."

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.934
-"Yeah, 'Aftersun' was great."
-Oh, my God.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.300
-You did that.
-I've done that before,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.734
and you go, "Oh, my God.
That's so rude."

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.400
But you're just nervous,

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.868
and "You get me
at the wrong moment."

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.667
-I have that happen so many
times to me at award shows.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.300
-But, no, the best thing,
I think,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.934
was you and Aubrey Plaza
at the SAG Awards.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:43.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.767
It was so -- it was so funny,
and it destroyed.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.300
It was a great bit.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.267
And then the Internet
went on fire.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.834
And it was, like, "We want
to see you guys in a movie.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.334
Do anything together.
Do something. Play sisters."

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.834
-Yeah, I would do anything
with her.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.234
She's another one of those
people where everyone

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.167
kept saying, "Oh, you remind me
of Aubrey,"

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.734
or, you know, "Oh, you two
should get together,"

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.968
and we just never did
until we were backstage then.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.300
And she just looked at me and
said, "Hey, you! Get over here."

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.667
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah!

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.267
See? Dude, she's so funny.
-Yeah, she was really cool.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.033
-She's smart.
She's everything, yeah.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.667
Can we talk about "Scream VI"?
-Yeah.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.634
-It's a big deal.
Tomorrow.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's out tomorrow.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.901
"Scream VI" is set in New York.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:18.968
Oh, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:21.868
New York City,
where we do our show.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.267
How do we set up this "Scream"?

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.734
-Well, this time,
it's kind of --

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.501
Well, yeah, it's a different
setting, which I mean,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.567
the "Scream" franchise
has never left Woodsboro,

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:34.267
so I think it makes for a lot
more an intimidating story,

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:35.601
I would say.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:38.167
You know, Ghostface
can come for you on the subway,

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.434
push you off
a skyscraper building.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:41.734
You know.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:43.133
-New York City
has got a lot of places.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:46.267
-Everything about this --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.367
I think everything about this
movie is just bigger

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.234
and scarier, and also Ghostface
is just so much more brutal.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.701
I feel like
he's very unforgiving,

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.767
and everyone's a victim,
not just the lead cast,

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.434
which makes it better.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.734
-Now, do you know
when you get the script,

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:01.601
do you know who Ghostface is,
or do they change the script

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.234
so that you don't really know
who it is?

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.000
-Sometimes they give us
different scripts,

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.100
different endings.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.667
This time around,
they just didn't give us

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:10.033
the third act at all.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:11.968
-So you gotta see the movie
to find out who the killer is?

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:13.634
-Yeah, now you just don't know.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.667
-Everyone usually finds out
at least by the last two weeks.

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:17.634
-Yeah.
-But they try to play games.

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.334
-Congrats on that,
and congrats on "SNL."

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:21.868
You're gonna be fantastic.
I want to show a clip.

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:24.133
Here's Jenna Ortega
in "Scream VI."

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.501
Take a look at this.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:27.400
-You and Tara
better watch your backs.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.567
-You better watch yours.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.801
-[ Gasps ]
-No!

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:32.934
-Unh!
[ Bike bell ring ]

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:35.834
-Come on!
Run!

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.534
Come on!

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.033
Help!
Please!

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:42.267
In there.

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:43.367
[ Door bell chimes ]

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:44.701
-Please!
Please help us!

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:46.133
-Please!
Call 911!

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.567
-There's a [bleep] line here,
girls.

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:48.634
[ Door bell chimes ]
-He's trying to kill us.

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.801
I'm telling you, sir!

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:51.934
♪♪

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.467
-You got a problem here, guy?

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.634
-Ooh!

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.133
Jenna Ortega!

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.734
"Scream VI"
is in theaters tomorrow.

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:05.033
Watch her host
"Saturday Night Live"

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:08.868
this weekend with musical guest
The 1975.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.300
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

